  "notes": "{寂|さび}しがる is a godan verb formed from the adjective {寂|さび}しい (lonely) + the suffix がる.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- Pattern: Xが{寂|さび}しがる / XがYを{寂|さび}しがる (X misses Y)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{寂|さび}しがっている describes someone visibly showing loneliness or missing someone.\n\nThe がる suffix is used to describe observable emotional states, particularly in third person:\n- {寂|さび}しい (I'm lonely) → {寂|さび}しがる (to show loneliness - typically third person)\n\nNote: Can also be spelled {淋|さび}しがる.\n\nRelated がる verbs:\n- {恥|は}ずかしがる (to show embarrassment)\n- {怖|こわ}がる (to show fear)\n- {欲|ほ}しがる (to show wanting)",
